  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Three",
      "h2": "Three Words for 'The'",
      "body_html": "<p>German nouns have three genders: <strong>der</strong> (masculine), <strong>die</strong> (feminine), <strong>das</strong> (neuter). 'Der Vater', 'die Mutter'. Learn the article with the noun.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Sibs",
      "h2": "Brothers & Sisters",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Der Bruder</strong> = brother. <strong>Die Schwester</strong> = sister. Plurals: <strong>die Bruder</strong>, <strong>die Schwestern</strong>. All nouns get capital letters in German.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Have",
      "h2": "Saying 'I Have'",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Ich habe</strong> = I have. 'Ich habe einen Bruder und zwei Schwestern' = 'I have one brother and two sisters'.</p>"
    }
